Arbor Vue Changes
----------------

Unreleased
----------

  * Stabilize stiff, highly connected spring layouts with adaptive physics steps
  * Add an interconnected demo preset and raise the demo-only limit to 100 nodes
  * Keep other nodes moving smoothly and the viewport stable during dragging
  * Expose friction in the demo and retain motion detection at maximum damping
  * Add demo controls for parking nodes, graph properties, and advanced physics
  * Add force-directed and hierarchical branching tree demo presets
  * Add Arbor-compatible energy, Point, Graphics, colors, Tween, and utility APIs
  * Synchronize edge length changes and support the documented tween ease option
  * Wake settled simulations when nodes or physics parameters change
  * Keep worker updates from overwriting newer node positions
  * Correct node hit testing on non-square canvases

Version 1.0.0
-------------

  * Migrated the package from Vue 2 / Vue CLI to Vue 3.5 / Vite
  * Added a Vue 3 canvas component with reactive graph and physics props
  * Restored graph APIs, canvas rendering, dragging, and data tweening
  * Added Barnes-Hut repulsion and an optional module Web Worker
  * Added ESM package exports, TypeScript declarations, and automated tests

Arbor.js Changes
----------------

Version 0.92 | 19 jun 2011
--------------------------

  * Creating nodes with an initial x/y or fixed position now works as advertised

  * Calling ParticleSystem's .screen() method without arguments will now 
    return an object with fields describing the current screen state

  * Fix for problems on chrome when running from file:// urls
  
  * Added a shell script to run a local http server so the demos will work without
    needing to be hosted somewhere

Version 0.91 | 17 jan 2011
--------------------------

  * Now supplementing brute-force repulsion calculations with the more-efficient
    (but noisier) barnes-hut algorithm. Use the ParticleSystem's .precision
    parameter to control the accuracy/speed trade-off.


Version 0.9 | 12 jan 2011
-------------------------

  * Initial release